.Dd October 31, 2026
.Dt TUCK 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tuck
.Nd tuck an idle system onto the low-power cores
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl hv
.Op Fl i Ar cpulist
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon saves power on systems with hybrid processors.  When the system
is nearly idle, it confines all tasks and movable interrupts to a few
low-power efficiency cores.  As soon as those low-power cores become a
bottleneck,
.Nm
gives every core back.
.Pp
To confine the system,
.Nm
creates a control group and assigns it with the CPUs in
.Ar cpulist ,
then turns it into an isolated cpuset partition.  The kernel will then
remove those CPUs from every other control group, so that all tasks
run on the remaining CPUs.  It also points the affinity of every
movable interrupt, and the default affinity of new ones, at the
remaining CPUs.
.Pp
.Nm
enters this idle state after the load average over all online CPUs are
monitered to be under 5% for 5 consecutive 1s samples.  It leaves this
state when the kernel reports through a pressure stall information
trigger that tasks waited for a CPU for at least 200ms within any 1s
window.
.Bl -tag
.It Fl h
Print the help message and exit.
.It Fl i Ar cpulist
Configure the CPUs to switch off while the system is idle, in the
kernel's cpulist format.
.It Fl v
Print every sample and evert step taken to standard error.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag
.It 0
Normal termination after a signal.
.It 1
Invalid option(s) or
.Ar cpulist ,
or failure to set up the control group.
.El
.Sh CAVEATS
Interrupt affinities are restored to all online CPUs, not to their
previous values.  Affinities set by hand or by a driver are lost after
the first confinement.
.Pp
Interrupts whose affinity are managed by the kernel itself, such as
NVMe queues, cannot be moved and are skipped.  They will only fire
when a task submits work from their CPU, which cannot happen when
confined.
.Pp
If another control group requests some of the CPUs in
.Ar cpulist ,
the partition becomes invalid.
.Pp
Tools that bind themselves to each CPU in turn, such as
.Xr turbostat 8 ,
cannot reach the switched-off CPUs while the system is confined.
